WEBVTT

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:10.450
What if the criminal was someone in the
palace who is nice to Your Highnesses?

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.290
Huh?

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.250
What if it was me?

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.790
The Pair's Promise

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.540
Master, a criminal?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.930
Don't make me laugh, Heine.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.700
Sheesh. Bruni, why are you
taking this seriously?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.820
It's a joke. You're supposed to laugh.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.330
What have I done?!

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:05.020
Forgive me! I did not realize it was a joke.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.760
I found out who you really are.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.850
What are we doing today?

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.660
If we're all here... A special lesson?

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.070
Are we going to town again?

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.490
A tabloid article?

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.800
"The fallen palace. A criminal
has slipped into the palace."

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.170
So claims this article.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.660
I would like you to investigate
the truth of this claim.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.830
Sounds like a waste of time.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:42.540
Yeah, I'm pretty busy.
I've got a date with some cute girls.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.410
It can't be true. We already know
the answer before investigating.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.690
It is true that tabloids are full of lies.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.020
However, assuming everything is a lie

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.190
is just as dangerous as believing
every rumor is true.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.510
Dangerous?

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.320
Say that you have become king,
and your successor is born.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:09.960
If you heard rumors of a criminal inside
the palace then, would you laugh it off?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.960
They could be targeting the successor.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:20.830
If you become king, a single error in
judgment could lose you this entire country.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:26.400
Of course, if Your Highnesses discover
it to be mere gossip, that is fine.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.970
Huh? Wait, what about you, Heine?

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:30.860
Are we investigating without you?

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:34.710
I have asked Ludwig and Maximilian to accompany you

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:38.070
if you need to leave the palace, naturally.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.990
I would like Your Highnesses to
verify the truth of the matter

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.410
and make a judgment yourselves,
as candidates for the throne.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.200
That is today's lesson.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:53.170
Okay, but what exactly do we do?

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.330
We'll meet with the person who wrote it.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:57.920
Huh?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.680
I get it! Asking the writer
would be the fastest.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.360
But who wrote it?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.540
There's no name on the article.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:09.670
I know who wrote the correction
article about me.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.710
I'll ask the newspaper company.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.180
Any luck?

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:17.590
He wasn't here.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.430
He was off today?

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.810
This is Gregor Klein. He wrote it.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.940
So that's our man.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.990
Right after he wrote it, he quit.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.150
He even moved. They don't know where he is.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.090
Huh? What's going on here?!

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.080
I don't know.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.580
The disappearance of someone who wrote
gossip about the royal family...

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.300
Maybe he quit as penance for
writing a rubbish article?

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.430
I hope that's the case.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.470
Bruni?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:47.680
Let's dig deeper.
Something about this is nagging at me.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.570
Me, too.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:49.810
But what do we investigate next?

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:53.430
We'll find Gregor, the article's author.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.440
Gregor's favorite store. His neighborhood.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.870
We interviewed so many people
and have nothing to show for it.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.120
I found him!

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:22.380
Truly?!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.430
Apparently he's been going to a local social
hall on the outskirts of town a lot lately.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:31.090
He changed his name to Karl Fischer, but he
looks basically the same as in this photo.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:34.400
They say he ranted about making
a fortune at a paper before.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.650
Amazing! How did you find that out?

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:39.950
A popular man has many
sources of information.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.900
Why did he change his name?

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.440
Kai...

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.400
That's Gregor?

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:54.820
So it seems.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.520
Gregor.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.890
You've got the wrong man. Excuse me.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:08.120
You wrote... my article...

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.790
Stop! Let me go!

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:15.250
What do you think you're doing?

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.790
We want to talk.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:22.220
You've got the wrong man.
I don't know any Gregor. My name is...

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.440
Karl Fischer.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.810
You sell yourself as a businessman
who recently came to Glanzreich.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.310
I took the liberty of looking
into the bank records.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.820
A bank account with a tidy sum
was opened under that name

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.330
the day after this article
was written, coincidentally.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.440
I don't know what you're on about.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.520
Maybe we should change the
carriage's destination.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.300
There's a cemetery deep
in the forest, right?

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:41.710
What?

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.420
You should know erasing you would be
a simple feat with our authority.

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.970
Hey, what's "authority"?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.670
We can erase this guy?

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:54.490
Ow!

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:55.190
Ahem.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.680
Tell us everything you know.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.100
Excuse me! To the forest, please!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.710
Okay! I'll talk! But I don't know much.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:07.940
I was told that I could make a fortune
if I wrote an article about the palace.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:08.760
By whom?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.920
A man I don't know. He approached
me on the street at night.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:13.290
What was he like?

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:17.200
He looked like a gentleman.
It was too dark to make out his face.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.120
He gave me money and said
the rest would go into an account

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.150
under the name Karl Fischer after
the article's publication.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:24.420
Told me to leave town and
do as I pleased with it.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.090
You didn't leave?

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.330
I've got no place to go.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.330
What about the claim that there
is a criminal in the palace?

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.580
That's a hoax.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.840
So it was false after all.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.710
Before the current king
ascended to the throne,

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.650
a criminal caused an incident
at the harvest festival.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:44.950
That criminal is now in the palace.
That's what he told me to turn into an article.

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:46.810
Before the king ascended?

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:49.960
Yeah. I wanted the money,
so I wrote the story.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.910
But there were no records of
it when I looked into it.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.370
You might not believe me,
but I do my research.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.020
That article is nonsense!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.220
Shh! Not so loud.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:06.040
Even we aren't supposed to be in
here without the king's permission.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.870
We'll be in big trouble if we get caught.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:12.750
Huh?

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.840
These are the records of all those

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.760
imprisoned during the harvest
festival prior to Father's coronation.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:20.010
A journalist could not
access these records.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.250
Are we going to look through all of these?

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:22.930
Of course.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.940
Licht, keep quiet.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:31.340
I'm starving. This is a waste of time.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.400
When we've finished, I'll feed you
as much sachertorte as you can eat.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:38.250
What is it?

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.400
Bruno, what was Heine's full name again?

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.170
Heine Wittgenstein.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:44.600
That can't be!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.200
What's the matter?

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:52.800
One Heine Wittgenstein was jailed
before Father took the throne.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.920
You're kidding me!

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.410
What was the crime?

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:56.820
Bruni?

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.410
Abduction and attempted
assassination of a prince.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.090
What does this mean?

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:06.520
He tried to kill our father.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.530
The year prior to Father's coronation,

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.440
someone was jailed for attempted
assassination of the prince...

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:15.320
and it was...

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.320
It was Heine?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.780
There's no way that's possible!
This must be some kind of mix-up.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.320
There could be two people with the same name!

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:28.080
Why did Master tell us to look into the
possibility of a criminal being in the palace?

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.940
If it was true, it could be dangerous.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.840
Would he really have us look into it then?

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:37.710
He wouldn't. He would never make us do
anything that would put us in harm's way...

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.700
Master knew we would be in no danger.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.280
Because the criminal is...

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.310
Heine.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.700
I'll ask him about it.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.020
Me, too!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:50.590
Wait!

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.480
Bruno!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.900
Don't let yourself in—

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:02.500
Heine?

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.870
At attention!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.160
Huh?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:15.170
Father. A thousand pardons for stopping you.
There is something we wish to ask you.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:19.920
What's this? No words of appreciation for
a king who's just finished his duties?

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:21.260
It's about Heine!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.830
You know something about
Heine's past, don't you?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.230
We want to know.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.590
About the professor...

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:33.280
Even if I did know, I could not tell you.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:37.580
Did Heine Wittgenstein
attempt to assassinate you?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.570
I have nothing to tell you.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.490
Father!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.150
Now, it's late. Return to your rooms.

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:46.250
We have to know!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:46.920
Dad!

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:49.830
Excuse me. A message for you.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:54.620
Father?

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.580
You are dismissed for the day.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.210
Understood.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:00.250
Sit, my boys.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.260
That's enough working for today.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:08.340
From this point on, I am not your king,
but your father.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.540
Let me tell you a story of the old days...

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.480
This was before I ascended to the throne.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:18.030
I would sneak out of the
palace from time to time.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:18.980
You did?!

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:20.670
Don't do this yourselves.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:28.230
I wanted to see the lives of the people
with my own eyes. To know their thoughts.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.490
I dressed myself as a commoner

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:33.170
and slipped out of the palace.

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:40.030
As long as I returned to my room in time
for the patrol, no one would know.

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.000
I'll make it cheap today!

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.690
Sorry!

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:54.640
Ah! Stop!

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:02.770
What'd we get?

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.130
What's this?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:06.980
I dunno, but I bet we
could get a lot for it.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:08.070
Good evening.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:11.570
Fancy seeing you again.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.830
Mind returning that?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:16.890
All right!

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.170
Get him!

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:20.630
That's enough.

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.050
Give it back to him.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.320
Aw, come on!

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.380
It seems really valuable!

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:33.020
I told you not to steal more than you need.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:33.920
But...

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:35.690
Return it!

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:37.530
Fine.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.630
Take your thing.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:44.940
You're not from here, are you?
Where did you come from?

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.340
Stay away from this area.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:53.910
Don't follow me.

00:12:58.350 --> 00:12:59.250
Tsk.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:10.260
You don't seem like one of us.
Are you a runaway?

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.770
You could say that.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:25.740
You <i>live</i> here?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.660
We do. It's not exactly unusual.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.990
Where are your parents?
Aren't they worried about you?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.150
What?

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.710
Did I say something funny?

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.470
None of the kids here have parents.
That's obvious.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:42.290
Even if they did, they'd all be
good-for-nothing scoundrels.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.510
You're an interesting one.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:50.680
Here.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.230
Once you've eaten, go home.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.890
This is a dangerous place for
a sheltered, pampered child.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.320
I am not a pampered...

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:20.630
I know I took a bite, but do you want it?

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.090
Here.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.140
Thank you!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.380
I was wrong about you.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.650
I'm Heine. Heine Wittgenstein.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.850
Viktor. Just Viktor.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:46.140
That was how I met Heine.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:52.830
After that, I would meet Heine
every time I snuck into town.

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.570
Heine was like the children's leader.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:15:00.110
He taught me many things, too.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.800
How to stay fed.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.540
How to find a warm place to sleep.

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:09.430
Everything necessary to get by.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.260
That there was a gap
between the rich and poor.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.260
The orphaned children worked
together to survive.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:19.540
I was rocked by the reality of my kingdom.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:23.710
What is it?

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.620
Don't make such a long face.
It's almost the harvest festival.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.330
A child bringing wine? That won't do.

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:33.510
I am not a child.

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:34.670
What kind of wine is it?

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:35.530
Dunno.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.620
It's written on the label!

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.640
Don't tell me you can't read.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:42.210
I don't particularly need to.

00:15:43.530 --> 00:15:46.610
White wine from Niederglanzreich?

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:50.190
Nieder... glanz... reich.

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:53.440
What?

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:54.280
Take it.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:55.650
I don't need your charity.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:57.920
It's not for you. It'll be winter soon.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.220
It's for the little kids
to get through the winter.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.240
If you sell it, you can buy
blankets and warm clothes.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.990
I don't want to see any dead bodies
when I get up in the morning.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:10.930
I'll trade you for that
Niederglanzreich white whine.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:13.270
This is my favorite.

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:15.530
You're too much of a kid to appreciate it.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.900
Your jokes are terrible.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.560
Thanks.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:28.250
One day, you'll all have
a warm place to sleep,

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.920
you'll never want for food,
and you'll have equal access to education.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.000
I want to make this a prosperous
and peaceful nation.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.490
When that happens, Heine, will you help me?

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:39.850
You say some funny things.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.810
Are you planning on becoming
king or something?

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:45.550
Well, if I could live in a dreamland
like that, I'd do anything.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:52.600
Heine was the one and only friend
to whom I could open my heart.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:58.070
Then, on the day of the harvest festival,
I slipped out of the palace as I always did.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.870
I didn't know

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.970
that the palace was in a
panic over my disappearance.

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:16.260
They believed that I had been kidnapped,
and leapt into action to find me.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.550
Let's go, Heine.

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:22.150
Huh?

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.100
You two! Stop!

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:31.640
This crest...

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:35.040
How did you get this, boy?!

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:37.730
We should run.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.450
The prince?!

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.370
That's the kidnapper? Stop!

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.500
Stop! Kidnapper!

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.000
He's not...

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.060
Vik... tor?

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.710
Hei... ne...

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:34.000
I-It's his fault! He used
the prince as a shield!

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:36.290
That brat used the prince as a shield!

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:37.530
What?!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:36.890
Vik...

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:42.300
Stop!

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:50.490
Stop...

00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.610
Heine!

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:04.480
Stop... Heine...

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.790
Viktor!

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.590
Heine...

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:11.450
Viktor.

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.000
Viktor!

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.080
Capture him!

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.570
Viktor!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:17.010
Viktor!

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:18.820
Viktor!

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:22.180
Viktor!

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:28.530
I came through, but I was
unconscious for days.

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:30.080
Meanwhile,

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:35.600
Heine was jailed for kidnapping and attempted
assassination of a prince for material gain.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:40.440
That was the first time Heine
learned of my station as prince.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:47.060
Heine never defended his innocence.
He only prayed.

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:54.780
Please save Viktor. I'll do anything...

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:09.500
I'm sorry it took me so long.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:16.390
I'm here for you, Heine.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.530
Thank God you're alive...

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.660
Your Highness...

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:30.230
I explained the truth to the king,
and Heine was pardoned.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:42.540
Later, I was crowned king.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:48.330
After a little while, I built a church
to shelter orphaned children.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.850
This is an important formula.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:52.850
Do you understand?

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.150
Heine became a teacher
for the children there.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.280
Heine, who could not even
read or write before,

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.720
became a teacher respected by all.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:06.330
He must have expended unimaginable effort.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:10.750
And so, I called him to the
palace to be the Royal Tutor.

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:12.280
This is the truth.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:17.040
Why did you tell us?
Isn't it a closely-guarded secret?

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:23.320
Of course it is. But unfounded rumors
about Heine might begin to circulate.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.300
I wanted you boys to know the truth.

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:29.560
Why would there be unfounded rumors?

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:34.800
I don't intend to make the truth public
and neither does Heine.

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:39.560
People will likely come up with fanciful gossip,
as with tabloid articles.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:43.930
Huh? But why won't you and
the professor explain?

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:46.730
Because this is a promise I made with Heine.

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:52.020
If his past became public, he would
immediately leave the palace without a word.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:52.950
What?

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:07.580
Heine has resigned from
the post of Royal Tutor.

00:23:39.650 --> 00:23:41.780
Professor, thank you for everything.

00:23:41.780 --> 00:23:44.750
I will never forget your teachings, Master!

00:23:44.750 --> 00:23:46.580
This can't be the end, right?

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:49.040
Just you watch, Heine. This is our answer!

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:53.730
Final Episode:
The Last Lesson

00:23:49.410 --> 00:23:51.670
Final episode, "The Last Lesson"!

00:23:51.670 --> 00:23:53.980
Now, you need a lesson!
